{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1793806224,"nonce":"wUcnF/wRqS7BH77v7lH4GGLBQ34=","message":"Phase A implementation is local and uncommitted. The website now has a searchable static index and separate Button, Input, Select, Dialog, Progress and Line Chart pages, each with Preview | Live | Code, canonical book content, prop/update models, keyboard guidance, CSS classes/state hooks and source downloads. Blocks remain planned.\n\nNative GIFs and WASM share compiled Rust fixtures, CSS and the default Hybrid theme with bundled Noto Sans. Recordings use 560x320 logical pixels at 2x density, stream 48 frames at 60ms, and include the supplied rounded SVG cursor with violet fill, white edge, cyan glow and a click pulse. Pointer scripts exercise real controls and assert the resulting values. Full PNG sequences remain in target/component-captures.\n\nThe worker owns WASM/UI/layout/GPU through new OffscreenCanvas constructors. The DOM runner shares initialization/render/input paths. The worker ticks the scheduler, preserves wheel coalescing, waits for first GPU submission completion before ready, pauses outside Live, and uses per-instance/sequence messages. Reset/retry/CSS changes create a new worker and transferable canvas. Host services cover focus, committed text/composition, clipboard, viewport/DPR and lifecycle. No silent main-thread fallback.\n\nThe existing build-web-examples tool has a separate catalog mode. It stages a versioned JS/CSS/WASM release plus SHA-256 manifest and checks per-component recording fingerprints. The Pages workflow stages and validates the catalog without invoking the existing gallery path for local catalog commands.\n\nValidation: all 6 recording interaction scripts passed on native Metal; 2 native density/annotation tests passed; 2 catalog page/route/source tests passed; 6 Node worker lifecycle/order/failure tests passed; the release wasm-pack bundle builds and vali